        "created_at": 1794502338.5678113
      },
      "rev_n_5_141a8c_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_141a8c_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_141a8c",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of trying to balance the sums directly, consider using a two-pointer technique to try and find a partition where the sums differ significantly. Start with pointers at both ends of the sorted array and move them towards each other, adjusting the partition point based on the sums of the elements on either side. If at any point the sums differ by more than the largest remaining element, you've found a valid partition. If the pointers meet without finding such a partition, return -1.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5339516996006227118",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_141a8c_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a22c99ba09",
        "created_at": 1794502355.802553
      },
      "rev_n_4_c46a9b_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_c46a9b_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_c46a9b",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of trying to partition the array directly, sort the array and then use a greedy approach to distribute the largest elements between two groups. This ensures that the difference between the sums of the two groups is minimized, making it easier to find a valid partition if one exists.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5339516996006227118",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_c46a9b_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_546cf136dc",
        "created_at": 1794502404.7236981
      },
      "rev_n_6_cbb829_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_cbb829_1",
        "node_id": "n_6_cbb829",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of trying to partition the array into two groups with equal sums, check if there exists any element that can be swapped with another element to make the sums unequal. If such an element exists, swap them and return the modified array. If no such element exists, return -1.",
